  "$comment": "Time's declarations (lib/time.js). Calendars, chronologies, temporal units and their conversions are Time's registries — a Martian sol, a lunar month and the Gregorian year are rows, not code. A place's time zone is Time's setting at the place (zoneSetting), resolved up the place tree like its calendar: a zone is assigned at a country, may be assigned at any subdivision or city under it, and a place under none is in defaultZone. `countryZones` names each seeded country's primary zone (an IANA name); an operator assigns the others where a country spans several. Lists an operator edited under the offer engine's old names (legacyLists) are merged once.",
